From 5165d0deea0e86924aa9f10189ff21fc6d316362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=B6rg=20Thalheim?= <joerg@thalheim.io>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:08:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(handlers): add network identity first factor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mesh VPN users are already authenticated by their source address:
a daemon on the Authelia host knows which node key owns it. Add an
optional passwordless first factor that resolves the client
address via a whois backend speaking the nginx auth_request
protocol over a unix socket (e.g. tinc-auth, tailscale nginx-auth)
and starts a one factor session for the user named by the
configured response header. Off by default:

    first_factor_network:
      enable: true
      socket: /run/tinc-auth.sock

The portal attempts it once on load and silently falls back to the
password form. Sessions carry a NetworkIdentity AMR (RFC 8176 pop,
swk). Regulation and session handling mirror the password factor.

Signed-off-by: Jörg Thalheim <joerg@thalheim.io>
